ding with  the new two-story wing at the very spot  where the 1970s extension once stood  inside the architects decided to make  the old villa the centerpiece of the new  atrium visitors can look forward to  stunning views into and out of the  private chambers of the original owner  and resident franz von lima  reaching down from the ceiling of the  atrium is a spectacular vortex shaped  installation by Olafur Eliasson  that reflects light and color like a  kaleidoscope it's a sculpture that  spirals up and down creating dynamic  with two functions on the one hand  visitors just arriving are drawn up  towards the galleries at the same time  the range and vibrancy of colors in the  panes of glass is a reference to the  world of painting especially the blue  rider group the Malibu in space on the  display light that's of horizon as well  as its established collection of early  modern painting the Newland Bock house  has also expanded its range of  Contemporary Art  this was the main reason for the 20%  increase in exhibition space the  building's dimensions are far from  overwhelming however and very much in  keeping with Foster's model of make it  more domestic he's in has certainly each  room has its own personal character it's  as if you're visiting an art lover  friend at home instead of having works  of art in a cold formal setting they're  presented to viewers in an intimate way  from the inside you can see not only the  art but also the facade of the new  extension the golden metal rods were a  conscious choice imagine different  colors black white whatever they would  see more out of place than this metal a  golden facade as the artworks and  installations inside likewise shot  while modern urban architecture is  smoothly incorporated into the  neoclassical buildings comprising  Munich's Art District this is the  exciting new thing is that the building  links the old and new in a dynamic yet  elegant way the lane pas house Villa is  reborn as the famous gallery and museum  are transplanted into the 21st century
 

